      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clendenin%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was incorporated in 1904 and named after the Clendenin family, an early pioneer family in the Kanawha River Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clendenin%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Coal and Coke railroad was built through Clendenin in 1893, which allowed the local logging industry to establish itself.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clendenin%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Clendenin is home to the site of the world's first petrochemical plant, which was built in 1920 by Union Carbide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clendenin%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early industrial growth in Clendenin was driven by the discovery of cannel coal and the drilling of gas wells.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
